      "writtenOn": "2025-01-24T16:23:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t believe that we need to be able to turn this on or off for each caller individually. I believe that what we need is the ability to turn this off during an online index triggered for an upgrade (not normal change update indexes). I think there is a simple solution with if statements if we pass in a shared system level \"isWriteEnabled\" AtomicBoolean (or other boolean container) reference to each H2Cache on construction. This boolean reference container would only be set to false during the online \"upgrade\" reindex. By setting the boolean in this container to false, all the H2Caches would see it and avoid writting during that period.",
      "parentUuid": "423468f0_95601af0",
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0a76fa17_b80fc970",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-24T16:35:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "H2CacheImpl already has an isOfflineReindex used to prevent \"touches\" during an offline re-index. I suggest that we replace that with an AtomicBoolean, and call it isWriteEnabled which can then be controlled at runtime, and set it to false during online and offline upgrades.",
      "parentUuid": "61c1bd73_2cd44ffe",
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f864ba2a_1bd589a2",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065256
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-28T11:41:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Such a central switch would cause also user-caused actions not to write to caches. This might cause performance degradations depending on the traffic and the duration of the online reindexing. Thus, one of our suggestions was to do that switch on an individual cache level to only make cache read-only that are typically causing issues during reindexing, which at least in our experience are the *diff* caches.",
      "parentUuid": "0a76fa17_b80fc970",
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "62f901d2_06aef438",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-05T18:11:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree with the idea that a single global switch might be too much. I think that it would be very feasable to still have a \"global\" switch per cache that can turn off writes for that cache during indexing. If someone is conerned that this will degrade their performance too much during online re-indexing, then they can choose to not use the feature.",
      "parentUuid": "f864ba2a_1bd589a2",
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
