      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-29T06:32:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, but that would still be possible with my change. This boolean could still be added to the writer or dependent on that boolean, the writer in the SQLStore could intermittently switched to the Noopwriter. Would it be OK for you to add this for now? The support for online reindexing could be added on top of this. Unfortunately, I don\u0027t have the time to do that for now, but we would urgently need this change.",
      "parentUuid": "62f901d2_06aef438",
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd3a947b_5eb993d1",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/ReadWriteSqlStore.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T23:04:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The naming here breaks inheritance models, i.e. when you inherit something, it should still be a form of that thing. Inheriting a RO object should not turn it into a writting object. You could rename the RO class to be ReadingSqlStore (or ReadSqlStore) to avoid this problem.\n\nTo be honest, this adds a lot of extra code and an interface to achieve something that could easily be done mostly by adding the following to 5 methods instead:\n\n if (!isWriteEnabled) {\n   return;\n }\n\nI am not sure that is worth it? \n\nWhile I am a fan of reducing class sizes, I am concerned that this affects readability a bit. With this approach I have to understand two classes that are very much linked together in order to get the full picture of how the RW class works. I feel this might actually make working on this much more difficult in the future.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5034550e_02d42fa4",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/ReadWriteSqlStore.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065256
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-24T07:33:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that this solution is not ideal. Using n if-statements and deciding on each call what to do also doesn\u0027t seem elegant. I would suggest to create a `SqlStore.Writer` interface and `SqlStore.NoopWriter` and `SqlStore.PersistentWriter` implementations that are instantiated on construction of the SqlStore. That would still get rid of inheritance in SqlStore.",
      "parentUuid": "bd3a947b_5eb993d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bd875375_1e95a283",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/ReadWriteSqlStore.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 3604707
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-05T18:11:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Frankly, I don\u0027t see the inelegance of adding the if() statements that I proposed. One way to reduce the code in a single class would be to add these if() statements in a super class which inherits from the SqlStore class. I don\u0027t think that is needed, but I do think that approach is much simpler than creating separate RO/RW classes along with an interface.",
      "parentUuid": "5034550e_02d42fa4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "d87cee17fb9d4c70d0665bbc1b5aebded121a741",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4690372f_735c433d",
        "filename": "java/com/google/gerrit/server/cache/h2/ReadWriteSqlStore.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1065256
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-07T14:22:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My hesitation about the if() statements comes from a scenario where a new write-method would be added to SQLStore and the developer might forget to add this if()-statement, i.e. I believe it is error prone. Thus, I was trying to find a way around that. I am aware that the current solution in this change adds complexity and also doesn\u0027t allow a switch between readonly and readwrite at runtime, which would be required for your request to make this work for online reindexing (without human interaction). And I am not happy about this as well.",
